{"pageId":"/pages/examples/@id","routeParams":{"id":"mixed-plugins"},"data":{"example":{"id":"mixed-plugins","title":"Mixed Plugins","description":"Demonstrates using multiple plugins together with path-based\nconflict resolution via pathMappings configuration.\nsrc/ files use JavaScript plugin, tutorials/ use YAML manifest.\n","rootPath":"/home/runner/work/functional-examples/functional-examples/examples/mixed-plugins","files":[{"absolutePath":"/home/runner/work/functional-examples/functional-examples/examples/mixed-plugins/README.md","relativePath":"README.md","raw":"# Mixed Plugins Example\n\nThis example demonstrates using multiple plugins together with conflict resolution via `pathMappings`.\n\n## Usage\n\n```bash\n# Scan and display examples\nnpx functional-examples scan\n\n# Output as JSON\nnpx functional-examples scan -f json\n```\n\n## The Problem\n\nWhen both JavaScript and YAML manifest plugins are active, they may both try to claim the same files:\n\n- JavaScript plugin claims any `.ts` file with frontmatter\n- YAML manifest plugin claims any directory with `meta.yml`\n\nIf a TypeScript file is inside a directory with `meta.yml`, both plugins want it.\n\n## The Solution: pathMappings\n\nUse `pathMappings` in your config to specify which extractor wins for each path pattern:\n\n<%= file('functional-examples.config.json') %>\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nmixed-plugins/\n├── src/                    # JavaScript plugin handles these\n│   └── utils.ts            # Has frontmatter metadata\n└── tutorials/              # YAML manifest plugin handles these\n    └── hello-world/\n        ├── meta.yml\n        └── index.ts\n```\n\n## Extractor Names\n\n- `javascript-extractor` — The JavaScript/TypeScript plugin\n- `meta-yml` — The YAML manifest plugin\n\nThese names are defined by each plugin and used in `pathMappings`.\n","parsed":"!undefined","hunks":"!undefined","language":"markdown","highlightedHtml":"<pre class=\"shiki blueprint\" style=\"background-color:#122a48f2;color:#e8edf4\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-markdown\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">#</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> Mixed Plugins Example</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">This example demonstrates using multiple plugins together with conflict resolution via </span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">pathMappings</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">##</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> Usage</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">```</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">bash</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6B8AAA;font-style:italic\"># Scan and display examples</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B8D8F0\">npx</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\"> functional-examples</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\"> scan</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6B8AAA;font-style:italic\"># Output as JSON</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B8D8F0\">npx</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\"> functional-examples</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\"> scan</span><span style=\"color:#D4A94E\"> -f</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\"> json</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">```</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">##</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> The Problem</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">When both JavaScript and YAML manifest plugins are active, they may both try to claim the same files:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">-</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> JavaScript plugin claims any </span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">.ts</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> file with frontmatter</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">-</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> YAML manifest plugin claims any directory with </span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">meta.yml</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">If a TypeScript file is inside a directory with </span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">meta.yml</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">, both plugins want it.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">##</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> The Solution: pathMappings</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">Use </span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">pathMappings</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> in your config to specify which extractor wins for each path pattern:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">&#x3C;%= file('functional-examples.config.json') %></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">##</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> Project Structure</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">```</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">mixed-plugins/</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">├── src/                    # JavaScript plugin handles these</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">│   └── utils.ts            # Has frontmatter metadata</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">└── tutorials/              # YAML manifest plugin handles these</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">    └── hello-world/</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">        ├── meta.yml</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">        └── index.ts</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">```</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">##</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> Extractor Names</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">-</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\"> `</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">javascript-extractor</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> — The JavaScript/TypeScript plugin</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">-</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\"> `</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">meta-yml</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> — The YAML manifest plugin</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">These names are defined by each plugin and used in </span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">pathMappings</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span></code></pre>"},{"absolutePath":"/home/runner/work/functional-examples/functional-examples/examples/mixed-plugins/demo.sh","relativePath":"demo.sh","raw":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Demonstrates multiple plugins with path-based conflict resolution\n\n# #_region scan\n# Scan — plugins auto-detected, pathMappings resolve conflicts\nnpx functional-examples scan\n# #_endregion scan\n\n# #_region json\n# View detailed output showing which extractor claimed each example\nnpx functional-examples scan -f json\n# #_endregion json\n","parsed":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Demonstrates multiple plugins with path-based conflict resolution\n\n# Scan — plugins auto-detected, pathMappings resolve conflicts\nnpx functional-examples scan\n\n# View detailed output showing which extractor claimed each example\nnpx functional-examples scan -f json\n","hunks":[{"id":"scan","content":"# Scan — plugins auto-detected, pathMappings resolve conflicts\nnpx functional-examples scan","startLine":4,"endLine":7},{"id":"json","content":"# View detailed output showing which extractor claimed each example\nnpx functional-examples scan -f json","startLine":9,"endLine":12}],"language":"bash","highlightedHtml":"<pre class=\"shiki blueprint\" style=\"background-color:#122a48f2;color:#e8edf4\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6B8AAA;font-style:italic\">#!/usr/bin/env bash</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6B8AAA;font-style:italic\"># Demonstrates multiple plugins with path-based conflict resolution</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6B8AAA;font-style:italic\"># Scan — plugins auto-detected, pathMappings resolve conflicts</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B8D8F0\">npx</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\"> functional-examples</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\"> scan</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6B8AAA;font-style:italic\"># View detailed output showing which extractor claimed each example</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B8D8F0\">npx</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\"> functional-examples</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\"> scan</span><span style=\"color:#D4A94E\"> -f</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\"> json</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span></code></pre>"},{"absolutePath":"/home/runner/work/functional-examples/functional-examples/examples/mixed-plugins/functional-examples.config.json","relativePath":"functional-examples.config.json","raw":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"./.functional-examples/schema.json\",\n  \"scan\": {\n    \"include\": [\"src/**/*\", \"tutorials/*\"],\n    \"exclude\": [\"**/node_modules/**\"]\n  },\n  \"pathMappings\": [\n    {\n      \"pattern\": \"src/**\",\n      \"extractor\": \"javascript-extractor\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"pattern\": \"tutorials/**\",\n      \"extractor\": \"meta-yml\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","parsed":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"./.functional-examples/schema.json\",\n  \"scan\": {\n    \"include\": [\"src/**/*\", \"tutorials/*\"],\n    \"exclude\": [\"**/node_modules/**\"]\n  },\n  \"pathMappings\": [\n    {\n      \"pattern\": \"src/**\",\n      \"extractor\": \"javascript-extractor\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"pattern\": \"tutorials/**\",\n      \"extractor\": \"meta-yml\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","hunks":[],"language":"json","highlightedHtml":"<pre class=\"shiki blueprint\" style=\"background-color:#122a48f2;color:#e8edf4\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-json\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">{</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">  \"</span><span style=\"color:#A8D0F0\">$schema</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">\"</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">:</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\"> \"</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\">./.functional-examples/schema.json</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">\"</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">  \"</span><span style=\"color:#A8D0F0\">scan</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">\"</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">:</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">    \"</span><span style=\"color:#A8D0F0\">include</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">\"</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">:</span><span style=